# CyberTools CDR Analyzer

Advanced Call Detail Record (CDR) analysis tool for authorized cybercrime
investigation and cyber cell use. Companion tool to
[CyberTools Log Analyzer](https://github.com/altafreza345-gif/cybertools-log-analyzer).

## Features

- Flexible CSV/Excel ingestion — auto-detects common column name variants
  used by different telecom operators (calling/called number, date/time,
  duration, call type, tower/cell ID, IMEI/IMSI)
- Per-number risk analysis (call volume, unique contacts, odd-hour activity)
- IMEI switch detection (same number using multiple handsets)
- Tower/cell activity summary
- Link analysis — top contact pairs (who talks to whom, how often)
- Heuristic risk scoring (LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH) with explained reasons
- Three report formats generated every run:
  - **PDF** — branded investigation report (CyberTools theme)
  - **TXT** — plain-text report
  - **XLSX** — 4-sheet workbook (Summary, Suspicious Numbers, Contact Pairs,
    and full Raw CDR Records) for further sorting/filtering by
    investigators/authorities

## Installation

### Linux / Kali Linux

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

> On Kali/Debian systems, if `pip install` refuses to run outside a venv
> with an "externally-managed-environment" error, either use the venv
> above (recommended) or run:
> `pip install -r requirements.txt --break-system-packages`

### Windows

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Usage

```bash
# Direct file path
python3 cdr_analyzer.py path/to/cdr.csv

# Or run with no argument — you'll be prompted for a path
# (works with drag-and-drop from your file manager too)
python3 cdr_analyzer.py
```

Reports are written to the `reports/` folder (PDF + TXT + XLSX, timestamped).

## Expected CDR columns (flexible naming supported)

| Standard field | Accepted aliases (case-insensitive) |
|---|---|
| calling_number | a_party, caller, calling_no, msisdn, a_number |
| called_number | b_party, callee, called_no, b_number, destination_number |
| date + time / datetime | call_date+call_time, start_datetime, timestamp |
| duration | call_duration, duration_sec |
| call_type | type, cdr_type, service_type |
| tower_id | cell_id, cellid, site_id, lac_cell |
| imei / imsi | imei_number, a_party_imei / imsi_number |

Only `calling_number`, `called_number`, and a date/time field are required —
everything else is optional.

## Branding

The PDF/report header uses `assets/cybertools_logo1.png`. Keep this folder
alongside `cdr_analyzer.py` when cloning or moving the project.

## Security & Privacy

Intended for **defensive/authorized investigation and educational use only**.
Only analyze CDR/IPDR data you are legally authorized to access. Do not
commit real subscriber data or case files to this (or any public) repository.

## Important Limitations

Risk scores and flags are **investigative context, not proof**. A number's
call pattern does not by itself establish identity or intent — verify all
findings through proper legal process before drawing conclusions.

